      "description": "`cpSync` preserves symlinks here because `verbatimSymlinks` is enabled, but the sandbox install later writes and prunes files beneath those paths. If an install directory (or a nested path such as `.claude/rules`) is an absolute symlink, the sandbox contains a link to the original destination, so a `--dry-run` can modify or delete real files outside the sandbox. Reject symlinks or ensure the sandbox copy cannot resolve to the original destinations.",
